Rating guidelines: A company that implements privacy-by-design, collects only strictly necessary data, never sells or monetizes customer data, employs robust end-to-end encryption, and rejects warrantless surveillance requests gets a 100. A company that adheres to standard industry privacy practices and regulatory mandates (GDPR, CCPA) with standard opt-out policies gets a 50. A company that engages in pervasive surveillance, sells personal or biometric data to brokers without consent, scrapes private communications to train models, or has catastrophic unencrypted breaches gets a 1.